'' See the source's header. ReadDotArgAsCall_ re-associates a leading-dot first
'' argument with the call in front of it; two shapes reached it wrong.
''
'' A single '( p )' after the inner name is LIFTED by ParseAmbiguous -- the shape it
'' handles for 'proc (x), y' -- so the head stays a bare member and the argument
'' arrives with no placeholder in front of it, where '( p, q )' stays an N_CALL and
'' leaves one. The missing placeholder is what tells the two apart.
''
'' A PLAIN callee was refused because the rewrite insisted the base carry its own
'' leading dot. It cannot simply be let through: 'mk.x' over a parameterless FUNCTION
'' returning a UDT is a real member access spelled identically, and fbc prints 42 for
'' it. Whether the member BOUND is what separates them, and the last two lines of the
'' source hold that case.
''
'' 'verify: ok' IS THE ARITY ASSERTION -- a five-argument call of a four-argument
'' procedure is exactly what the verifier reported, seven times, on AfxNova's
'' CImageCtx. '0 statements not lowered' is the other half: spelling C declined
'' outright and its line printed nothing. What the arguments ARE is differenced
'' against fbc by build/goldenrun.sh.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/dot-arg-statement-call.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
